inclusion.GLOBAL_I3:
Permitted contrast types- the analysis must be ONE of the following five, which are the only contrast types this benchmark admits- (1) a problem solving task minus a baseline or control condition; (2) a parametric or categorical comparison across difficulty, abstraction or complexity
    (e.g. complex > simple, multi-digit > single-digit, high > low load, 2-relational >
    1-relational, a positive linear trend with problem depth);
(3) untrained, novel or previously unseen problems > trained, memorized or previously
    solved problems of the same type;
(4) one type of problem solving > another type, across rule sets or representational
    modalities (e.g. multiplication > addition, word problems > number problems);
(5) one problem solving phase > another, sequential phase (e.g. late > early, solution >
    preparation).
